$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Aldehyde carbonate (±)-12: To a stirred solution of hydroxy carbonate
(±)-20-1 (0.60 g, 1.07 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (10 mL) at 25°C was added
PhI(OAc)2 (2.0 equiv, 0.68 g, 2.14 mmol) and TEMPO (1.0 equiv, 0.16 g,
1.07 mmol). The resulting mixture was stirred for 16 h and then quenched
with a mixture of saturated aqueous solution of NaHCO3 (10 mL) and
Na2S2O3 (10 mL). The resulting mixture was extracted with Et2O (2 × 10
mL), dried (MgSO4), and concentrated in vacuo. The crude residue was
purified by flash column chromatography (silica, EtOAc/hexanes, 5 → 20%)
to furnish aldehyde carbonate (±)-12 (0.54 g, 0.97 mmol, 90%). compound
(±)-12, yield (0.54 g, 0.97 mmol, 90%). Rf = 0.50 (silica, Et2O:hexanes,
1:1); IR (film): νmax = 2951m, 1752s, 1716s, 1441m, 1266m, 1041s cm-1; 1H
NMR (C6D6, 500 MHz): δ = 9.72 (s, 1 H), 7.33 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 2 H), 7.18
(d, J = 7.0 Hz, 1 H), 7.09 (t, J = 7.0 Hz, 1 H), 5.94 (s, 1 H), 5.59 (d,
J = 1.5 Hz, 1 H), 4.55 (d, J = 12.0 Hz, 1 H), 4.57 (s, 2 H), 4.43 (d, J =
12.0 Hz, 1 H), 4.41 (s, 1 H), 4.03 (d, J = 11.0 Hz, 1 H), 4.01 (d, J =
3.5 Hz, 1 H), 3.85 (dd, J = 11.0, 1.0 Hz, 1 H), 3.42 (s, 3 H), 2.58 (ddd,
J = 9.5, 6.0, 5.0 Hz, 1 H), 2.46 - 2.34 (m, 3 H), 2.23 (d, J = 3.5 Hz, 1
H), 2.20 - 2.07 (m, 3 H), 1.97 - 1.78 (m, 3 H), 1.81 - 1.56 (m, 6 H),
1.46 (ddd, J = 9.5, 6.0, 4.5 Hz, 1 H), 1.30 (m, 1 H), 1.26 (s, 3 H), 1.18
(s, 3 H) ppm; 13C NMR (C6D6, 125 MHz): δ = 199.30, 155.36, 143.26,
138.53, 128.65, 123.92, 99.26, 95.79, 77.48, 77.40, 75.45, 70.29, 67.19,
66.18, 63.13, 54.86, 54.77, 49.85, 36.03, 33.76, 31.83, 29.67, 26.30,
24.45, 24.27, 22.56, 22.14, 20.06 ppm; HRMS calcd for C32H42O8H+ [M + H+]
577.2772 found 577.2775.
