$DATUM (R,E)-5-((tert-Butyldiphenylsilyl)oxy)-2,4-dimethylpent-2-enal (11).
TEMPO (4 mg, 0.028 mmol) was added to a solution of the starting allylic
alcohol (0.295 g, 0.56 mmol), BAIB (0.361 g, 1.13 mmol), and NaHCO3
(0.376 g, 4.48 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (5 mL) at room temperature. The yellow
orange solution was stirred at room temperature overnight. The reaction
was then quenched by the simultaneous addition of aqueous pH 7 buffer and
aqueous saturated sodium thiosulfate. The layers were separated and the
aqueous layer was extracted three times with CH2Cl2. The combined organic
layers were dried over Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo to
yield a pale yellow solid which was purified by column chromatography
(using a gradient of 100:0 - 97:3, hexanes/EtOAc) to yield aldehyde 11.
Colorless oil, yield 0.193 g, 0.504 mmol, 90%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ
(ppm): 9.36 (s, 1H), 7.65 - 7.63 (m, 4H), 7.45 - 7.36 (m, 6H), 6.28 (dd,
J = 9.8, 2.2 Hz, 1H), 3.66 (dd, J = 9.8, 5.5 Hz, 1H), 3.59 (dd, J = 9.7,
6.6 Hz, 1H), 2.98 - 2.88 (m, 1H), 1.72 (d, J = 1.2 Hz, 3H), 1.07 (d, J =
7.1 Hz, 3H), 1.04 (s, 9H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm): 195.4,
157.1, 139.2, 135.6, 135.5, 133.4, 133.4, 18.7, 128.7, 127.7, 67.5, 36.4,
26.8, 19.2, 16.0, 9.4.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM literature preparation, buffered solution used in stage 2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Stereocontrol in Asymmetric SE' Reactions of γ-Substituted
α,β-Unsaturated Aldehydes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
