$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of lactol 16 (4.0 g, 11.9 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (40 mL) at 0 °C
was added TEMPO (185 mg, 1.19 mmol) followed by iodobenzene diacetate
(5.75 g, 17.85 mmol) and allowed the reaction mixture to stirred at
ambient temperature for 4 h. After conversion of the diol completely to
lactone, reaction mixture was quenched with saturated solution of Sodium
thiosulfate (5 mL) and extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 x 50 mL). The combined
organic layers were dried over Na2SO4 and evaporation of solvent under
reduced pressure led to the crude lactone which was purified on silica
gel column chromatography to furnish the lactone 17.
(R)-2-((2R,3R,4S,5S)-4-(Benzyloxy)-3,5-dimethyl-6-oxotetrahydro-2H-pyran-2-yl)propyl
acetate (17). Colorless viscous liquid, yield (3.57 g, 90%). Rf = 0.40
(hexanes:EtOAc, 7:3); [α] D 28 = -38.5 (c 1, CHCl3); IR (neat) ν max:
3461, 2922, 2852, 1723, 1458, 1273, 1110, 988, 715 cm-1; 1H NMR (300 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 7.36-7.22 (m, 5H), 4.53 (ABq, J= 11.3 Hz, 2H), 4.32 (m, 1H),
4.10 (dd, J = 5.2, 11.3 Hz, 1H), 4.0-3.9 (m, 2H), 2.92-2.82 (m, 1H),
2.48-2.37 (m, 1H), 2.20-2.09 (m, 1H), 2.04 (s, 3H), 1.31 (d, J = 7.5 Hz,
3H), 0.98-0.92 (m, 6H) ppm; 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ 174.1, 170.9,
137.6, 128.3, 127.7, 127.3, 78.7, 75.8, 72.4, 65.5, 38.2, 33.8, 32.7,
20.8, 12.8, 12.2, 6.1 ppm; HRMS calculated for C19H26O5Na [M+Na]+
357.1688, found 357.1677.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Formation of Substituted Tetrahydropyrans through Oxetane Ring Opening:
Application to the Synthesis of C1-C17 Fragment of Salinomycin
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Yadav, J. S.; Singh, Vinay K.; Srihari, P.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2014), 16(3), 836-839

