$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for oxidation of alcohols to aldehydes: To an
oven-dried roundbottom flask containing a 23 °C solution of the
appropriate alcohol (1.0 equiv) and CH2Cl2 (0.5 M) was added iodobenzene
diacetate (1.05 equiv) and TEMPO (0.1 equiv). The solution stirred for 14
h. and was quenched by the addition of 1.0 M Na2S2O3 aqueous solution.
After 10 minutes of vigorous stirring, the aqueous layer was extracted
with CH2Cl2 (2x). The combined organic layers were washed with saturated
NaHCO3 (1x), brine (1x) and were dried with Na2SO4, filtered, and
concentrated. Purification by flash column chromatography afforded the
desired aldehyde. 2-(1-tosylpiperidin-4-yl)acetaldehyde: Prepared
following the general procedure outlined above with
2-(1-tosylpiperidin-4-yl)ethanol (3.6 g, 12.70 mmol), Iodobenzene
diacetate (4.3 g, 13.34 mmol), TEMPO (198 mg, 1.270 mmol) and
dichloromethane (25.4 mL). Purification by flash column chromatography
using 25% to 75% ethyl acetate in hexanes gradient afforded
2-(1-tosylpiperidin-4-yl)acetaldehyde (3.2 g, 11.37 mmol, 90% yield) as
white solids. IR (thin film, cm-1) ν 2921, 2845, 1721, 1597, 1446, 1336,
1306, 1246, 1163, 1094, 1050, 932, 817, 726. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ
9.72 (t, J = 1.3 Hz, 1H), 7.63 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 2H), 7.32 (d, J = 7.9 Hz,
2H), 3.75 (m, 2H), 2.44 (s, 3H), 2.38 (dd, J = 6.6, 1.5 Hz, 2H), 2.26
(td, J = 12.0, 2.5 Hz, 2H), 1.75 (m, 3H), 1.37 (m, 2H). 13C NMR (126 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 200.98, 143.52, 132.77, 129.60, 127.68, 49.85, 46.17, 31.19,
29.55, 21.54. HRMS (ESI-TOF) Calculated for C14H19NO3S [M+H]: 282.11639
Found: 282.11579
