$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (S,E)-tert-Butyl
2-(2-methyl-3-oxoprop-1-en-1-yl)pyrrolidine-1-carboxylate (15, R = CH3).
TEMPO (4 mg, 0.026 mmol) was added to a solution of 38 (R = CH3) (0.126
g, 0.522 mmol), BAIB (0.420 g, 1.31 mmol), and NaHCO3 (0.439 g, 5.22
mmol) at room temperature. The yellow orange solution was stirred at room
temperature overnight. The reaction was then quenched by the simultaneous
addition of aqueous pH 7 buffer and aqueous saturated sodium thiosulfate.
The layers were separated and the aqueous layer was extracted three times
with CH2Cl2. The combined organic layers were dried over Na2SO4,
filtered, and concentrated in vacuo to yield a yellow solid which was
purified by silica gel column chromatography using a gradient elution
(hexanes/EtOAc, 100:0 - 85:15 by volume) to yield aldehyde 15 (R = CH3)
which solidified into a low melting solid upon standing at -20 °C
overnight. Pale yellow oil, yield 0.105 g, 0.470 mmol, 90%. Rf = 0.27
(80:20 hexanes:EtOAc by volume); [α]D22 +15.0 (c 0.38, CHCl3); 1H NMR
(500 MHz, CDCl3, 323.1 K) δ (ppm): 9.40 (s, 1H), 6.35 (d, J = 8.3 Hz,
1H), 4.67 (br s, 1H), 3.53 (s, 1H), 3.48 - 3.43 (m, 1H), 2.25 - 2.19 (m,
1H), 1.99 - 1.85 (m, 2H), 1.81 (s, 3H), 1.74 - 1.68 (m, 1H), 1.41 (s,
9H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3, 323.1 K) δ (ppm): 194.5, 154.9, 154.3,
137.8, 79.7, 55.4, 46.6, 32.3, 28.4, 24.1, 9.1; HRMS-CI (calc. for
C13H21NO3 [M+H]+) 240.1600, found 240.1585.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM buffered solution used in stage 2
