$DATUM (S)-5-((tert-butyldimethylsilyloxy)methyl)-1-(4,5-dimethoxy-2-nitrobenzoyl)pyrrolidin-3-one
TEMPO (0.32 g, 2.06 mmol, 0.1 Equiv.) and BAIB (7.33 g, 22.75 mmol, 1.1
Equiv.) were added to a solution of S145 (9.1 g, 20.68 mmol, 1.0 Equiv.)
in DCM (200 mL) and the mixture was stirred for 2 h when TLC
(EtOAc/hexane 1:1) indicated complete consumption of starting material.
The reaction mixture was then diluted with DCM (100 mL) and washed with
an aqueous saturated solution of Na2S2O3 (200 mL). The aqueous layer was
extracted with DCM (2 x 200 mL) and the combined organic layers were
washed with brine (200 mL) and dried over MgSO4. Removal of excess
solvent under reduced pressure afforded a solid which was purified by
flash column chromatography (EtOAc/hexane 1:1) to afford compound S15
(8.2 g, 90%).
(S)-5-((tert-butyldimethylsilyloxy)methyl)-1-(4,5-dimethoxy-2-nitrobenzoyl)pyrrolidin-3-one,
yield (8.2 g, 90%). [α]27 D = - 130o (c = 0.13, CHCl3). IR (film,
νmax/cm-1): 3020, 2932, 2862, 1769, 1645, 1582, 1526, 1464, 1428, 1338,
1278, 1216, 1102, 1060, 1014, 871, 838, 769, 668. 1H-NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz)
rotamers: δ 0.22 (two s, 6 H, Si(CH3)2), 0.86 (s, 9 H, C(CH3)3), 2.55 (d,
1 H, J = 17.9 Hz, H1β ), 2.79 (dd, 1 H, J = 9.3, 17.7 Hz, H1β ), 3.45 (d,
1 H, J = 17.4 Hz, H3), 3.65 (d, 1 H, J = 17.4 Hz, H3), 3.72 (dd, 1 H, J =
2.0, 10.2 Hz, H11a), 3.96 (s, 3 H, 7-OCH3), 3.99 (s, 3 H, 8-OCH3), 4.31
(dd, 1 H, J = 1.80, 10.2 Hz, H11), 4.98 (d, 1 H, J = 8.9 Hz, H11), 6.75
(s, 1 H, H6), 7.72 (s, 1 H, H9). 13C-NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz) rotamers: δ
208.1 (C2), 166.5 (C5), 166.3 (C5), 154.4 (C7), 149.5 (C8), 137.5 (C9a),
126.9 (C5a), 108.6 (C9), 107.2 (C6), 65.0 (C11), 56.6 (C11a), 56.5, 55.1,
55.0 (7-OCH3, 8-OCH3 and C3), 40.0 (C1), 25.7 (C(CH3)3), 18.1 (Cquat),
-5.6 (SiCH3)2). MS (ESI+) m/z (relative intensity): 439.0 ([M + H]+,
48%).
