$DATUM (1S,3'S,5S)-1'-methoxy-2',9-dioxo-6-oxaspiro[bicyclo[3.2.2]non[2]ene-4,3'-indoline]-2-carbaldehyde
(18) To a stirred solution of S2 (4.63 g, 14.7 mmol) and PhI(OAc)2 (10.4
g, 32.3 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (73 mL) at room temperature was added TEMPO (461
mg, 2.94 mmol). After stirring for 3 h, the reaction mixture was diluted
with 50% EtOAc in n-hexane (100 mL) and saturated NaHCO3 aq. (50 mL). The
slurry was filtered through a pad of Celite and the filter cake was
washed with 50% EtOAc in n-hexane (20 mL) seven times and the filtrate
was partitioned between 50% EtOAc in n-hexane (30 mL) and H2O (25 mL).
The organic phase was collected and the aqueous phase was extracted with
50% EtOAc in n-hexane (50 mL) twice. The combined organic extract was
washed with brine (50 mL), dried over MgSO4, filtered and concentrated in
vacuo. The residue was purified by flash column chromatography on silica
gel (n-hexane/EtOAc = 3/1 to 2/1) to afford 18. Pale yellow foam, yield
4.15 g, 13.2 mmol, 90%. Rf = 0.41 (n-hexane/EtOAc = 1:1, UV, Ce-PMA);
[α]23D -48.6 (c = 1.00, CHCl3); IR (neat, cm-1 ) 2925, 1742, 1688, 1645,
1614, 1464, 1320, 1213; 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 9.46 (s, 1H), 7.44 (dd,
7.8, 7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.37 (d, J = 7.4 Hz, 1H), 7.16 (dd, J = 7.8, 7.8 Hz,
1H), 7.09 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 6.25 (s, 1H), 4.22 (d, J = 10.1 Hz, 1H),
4.18 (d, J = 10.1 Hz, 1H), 4.06 (s, 3H), 3.89 (s, 1H), 3.76 (m, 1H), 2.86
(d, J = 19.2 Hz, 1H), 2.77 (dd, J = 19.2, 5.0 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (CDCl3,
100 MHz) δ 202.3, 191.2, 167.1, 149.2, 146.1, 139.3, 130.0, 126.4, 124.8,
123.8, 108.1, 81.0, 69.8, 64.0, 58.3, 42.7, 26.1; HRMS (ESI) calcd for
C17H15NO5 ([M+Na]+) 336.0848, found 336.0845.
