$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2.2.2 Oxidation of Alcohols with (PhIO)3•SO3 Generated In Situ
β-Cyclodextrin (0.57 g, 0.5 mmol) was dissolved in H2O (15 mL) at 60 °C
for several minutes, followed by addition of alcohol (1 mmol) with
stirring. Then PhI(OAc)2 (0.35 g, 1.1 mmol) and NaHSO4.H2O (0.15 g, 1.1
mmol) were added and stirred at 60 °C for several hours while checking
the reaction progress by gas or thin-layer chromatography. After the
completion of the reaction, the mixture obtained was treated as above to
afford the corresponding pure product. Table 2. Entry 6, yield 89%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, green chemistry, selective oxidation to aldehyde (no
over-oxidation), (PhIO)3*SO3 as oxidant gave similar yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Simple and Highly Selective Biomimetic Oxidation of Alcohols with
Hypervalent Iodine(III) Reagent Catalyzed by β-Cyclodextrin in Water
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zhu, Chenjie; Wei, Yunyang
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Catalysis Letters (2011), 141(4), 582-586

