$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Procedure C. To a solution of alcohol (1.0 equiv) in CH2Cl2 (0.1 M) was
added iodobenzene diacetate (BAIB) (3.0 equiv) and TEMPO (0.3 equiv) at
0°C. After 0.5 h at this temperature, a saturated aqueous Na2S2O3
solution was added and the bilayer system was allowed to stir at 0°C for
an additional 0.5 h. The organic phase was then separated, the aqueous
layer extracted with CH2Cl2 (twice), and the combined organic extracts
were washed with brine, dried (MgSO4) and filtered. After concentration
under reduced pressure, the crude aldehyde was purified by flash column
chromatography (silica gel, 5% AcOEt in hexanes) to provide the
corresponding aldehyde. Aldehyde 66. Obtained by procedure C in a 89% as
a colorless oil: Aldehyde 66, yield 265 mg, 89% Rf = 0.49 (silica gel,
10% EtOAc in hexanes); [α]D25 = +15.0 (c = 1.0, CH2Cl2); 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = 0.11 (s, 6 H), 0.74 (d, J = 6.3 Hz, 3 H), 0.89 (d, J = 7.0
Hz, 3 H), 0.92 (s, 9 H), 1.14 (d, J = 6.7 Hz, 3 H), 1.37 and 1.44 (2 s, 6
H), 1.83-1.95 (m, 2 H), 2.74- 2.81 (m, 1 H), 3.54 (dd, J = 11.1 Hz, 1 H),
3.66 (d, J = 10.1 Hz, 1 H), 3.73 (dd, J = 11.2, 4.8 Hz, 1 H), 3.99 (d, J
= 5.0 Hz, 1 H), 9.85 (d, J = 2.0 Hz, 1 H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ =
-4.4, 8.4, 11.3, 12.7, 18.1, 19.5, 25.8, 29.6, 30.2, 39.7, 50.5, 66.0,
74.9, 77.0, 97.8, 204.4.
