$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Hydroxy aldehyde (-)-99-1: To a stirred solution of diol (+)-99 (146 mg,
0.185 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (5 mL) at 25°C were added PhI(OAc)2 (5.0 equiv, 300
mg, 0.92 mmol) and TEMPO (2.0 equiv, 58 mg, 0.37 mmol). The reaction
mixture was stirred at 25°C for 36 h and then quenched sequentially with
saturated aqueous solutions of Na2S2O3 (5 mL) and NaHCO3 (5 mL). The
resulting mixture was extracted with Et2O (2 × 10 mL), dried (MgSO4), and
concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude residue was purified by
flash column chromatography (silica, EtOAc/hexanes, 5 → 10%) to afford
hydroxy aldehyde (-)-99-1 (130 mg, 0.165, 89%) as a white foam. compound
(-)-99-1, yield (130 mg, 0.165, 89%). Rf = 0.30 (silica, Et2O:hexanes,
1:3); [α]25 D = -43.91 (c = 0.23, CHCl3); IR (film): νmax = 3508brs,
2946m, 2875m, 1705m, 1456w, 1376w, 1246w, 1055s cm-1; 1H NMR (C6D6, 600
MHz): δ = 10.31 (s, 1 H), 5.55 (s, 1 H), 4.88 (s, 1 H), 4.87 (d, J = 7.8
Hz, 1 H), 4.84 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1 H), 4.54 (s, 1 H), 4.27 (d, J = 2.4 Hz,
1 H), 4.07 (s, 1 H), 3.81 (t, J = 3.0 Hz, 1 H), 3.79 - 3.74 (m, 2 H),
2.50 (m, 1 H), 2.30 (m, 1 H), 2.22 (d, J = 3.6 Hz, 1 H), 2.22 - 2.06 (m,
5 H), 1.95 - 1.89 (m, 2 H), 1.86 - 1.80 (m, 2 H), 1.77 (m, 2 H), 1.61 (m,
1 H), 1.59 (s, 3 H), 1.55 - 1.48 (m, 2 H), 1.48 (s, 3 H), 1.42 (s, 3 H),
1.39 (s, 3 H), 1.38 (s, 3 H), 1.22 (m, 2 H), 1.02 (t, J = 7.8 Hz, 9 H),
1.00 (m, 2 H), 0.66 (q, J = 7.8 Hz, 6 H), 0.02 (s, 9 H) ppm; 13C NMR
(C6D6, 150 MHz): δ = 200.04, 151.27, 144.27, 116.70, 111.92, 98.88,
89.33, 77.58, 75.45, 75.18, 73.07, 70.46, 64.87, 57.38, 53.90, 52.50,
52.32, 51.90, 51.33, 50.35, 43.20, 38.07, 32.77, 30.02, 28.09, 26.67,
25.98, 25.23, 25.20, 23.78, 23.72, 23.64, 22.26, 18.42, 7.25, 5.36, -1.24
ppm; HRMS calcd for C45H76O7Si2H+ [M + H+] 785.5202 found 785.5192.
