$DATUM (S,E)-4-((tert-Butyldiphenylsilyl)oxy)-2-methylpent-2-enal (12): TEMPO (3
mg, 0.022 mmol) was added to a solution of the starting alcohol (0.156 g,
0.445 mmol), BAIB (0.287 g, 0.89 mmol), and NaHCO3 (0.299 g, 3.56 mmol)
in CH2Cl2 (5 mL) at room temperature. The yellow orange solution was
stirred at room temperature overnight. The reaction was then quenched by
the simultaneous addition of aqueous pH 7 buffer and aqueous saturated
sodium thiosulfate. The layers were separated and the aqueous layer was
extracted three times with CH2Cl2. The combined organic layers were dried
over Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo to yield a pale yellow
solid which was purified by column chromatography (using a gradient of
100:0 - 96:4, hexanes/EtOAc) to yield aldehyde 12. Colorless oil, yield
0.140 g, 0.396 mmol, 89%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm): 9.29 (s, 1H),
7.68 - 7.60 (m, 4H), 7.46 - 7.31 (m, 6H), 6.40 (dq, J = 8.2, 1.1 Hz, 1H),
4.76 - 4.70 (m, 1H), 1.34 (d, J = 1.1 Hz, 3H), 1.27 (d, J = 5.9 Hz, 3H),
1.07 (s, 9H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM literature preparation, buffered solution used in stage 2
