$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Spiro Aldehyde- 17: To a stirred solution of diol 16 (38 mg, 0.127 mmol)
in DCM (3 mL) at 0°C was added iodobenzenediacetate (49.2 mg, 0.153mmol)
followed by TEMPO (2 mg, 0.0128 mmol) and allowed the reaction mixture to
stir at ambient temperature for 3h. After this reaction mixture was
quenched with saturated aqueous solution of hypo and extracted with DCM
(3x10 mL) and the combined organic layers were dried, evaporated under
reduced pressure and the residue was purified on silica gel using 10%
EtOAc/hexanes to furnish the aldehyde 17 (33.5 mg, 89%). Rf = 0.4 (20%
EtOAc/hexane). [α]25 D : -20.5 (c = 0.4, CHCl3); IR (KBr) 3450, 3020,
2850, 2730, 1730, 1100, 1120 cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 9.76 (d, J =
2.7 Hz, 1H), 5.99 (dd, J = 10.2, 5.6 Hz, 1H), 5.53 (d, J = 10.2 Hz, 1H),
4.15 (dd, J = 10.4, 1.7 Hz, 1H), 3.98-3.85 (m, 2H), 2.71-2.50 (m, 1H),
2.09-1.97 (m, 1H), 1.71-1.56 (m, 2H), 1.50 (quin, J = 7.3 Hz, 2H), 1.25
(m, 3H), 1.00-0.85 (m, 12H). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75 MHz): δ 205.4, 130.4,
127.2, 97.0, 72.2, 71.9, 71.5, 47.7, 40.7, 40.3, 35.9, 26.1, 22.3, 12.4,
11.8, 9.6, 4.5. MS-ESI (m/z) [M+Na] +: 319.1; HRMS: calculated for
C17H28O4 Na [M+Na] + 319.1885 found 319.1889.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
