$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Acetoxy aldehyde (+)-108: To a stirred solution of diol (-)-107 (50 mg,
0.050 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (2.3 mL) at 25 °C was added PhI(OAc)2 (64 mg, 0.199
mmol) and TEMPO (15.5 mg, 0.10 mmol). The reaction mixture was stirred at
25 °C for 15 h and then quenched with saturated aqueous solutions of
Na2S2O3 (2 mL) and NaHCO3 (2 mL). The resulting mixture was extracted
with Et2O (2 x 10 mL), dried (MgSO4), and concentrated under reduced
pressure. The crude residue was purified by flash column chromatography
(silica, EtOAc/hexanes, 4 - 11%) to afford the corresponding hydroxy
aldehyde, yield 44 mg, 0.044 mmol, 88%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
