$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Aldehyde 18. To a solution of alcohol 17 (477
mg, 1.00 mmol, 1.0 equiv) in CH2Cl2 (30 mL) was added iodobenzene
diacetate (BAIB) (966 mg, 3.00 mmol, 3.0 equiv) and TEMPO (45.6 mg, 0.30
mmol, 0.3 equiv) at 0°C. After 0.5 h at this temperature, a saturated
aqueous Na2S2O3 solution was added and the bilayer system was allowed to
stir at 0°C for an additional 0.5 h. The organic phase was then
separated, the aqueous layer extracted with CH2Cl2 (2 x 10 mL), and the
combined organic extracts were washed with brine, dried (MgSO4) and
filtered. After concentration under reduced pressure, the crude aldehyde
was purified by flash column chromatography (silica gel, 5% AcOEt in
hexanes) to obtain aldehyde 18 (465 mg, 98%) as a colorless oil Aldehyde
79. The oxidation of alcohol 78 (66 mg, 0.12 mmol) was carried out
exactly as described for 18, by treatment with BAIB (120 mg, 0.37 mmol,
3.0 equiv) in the presence of TEMPO (5.5 mg, 0.037 mmol, 0.3 equiv), to
obtain, after purification by flash column chromatography (silica gel,
2.5% AcOEt in hexanes), aldehyde 79 (54 mg, 85%) as a colorless oil: Rf =
0.54 (silica gel, 10% EtOAc in hexanes); [α]D25 = -46.8 (c = 1.4,
CH2Cl2); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 0.02 (s, 9 H), 0.03 (s, 3 H), 0.65
(d, J = 6.6 Hz, 3 H), 0.81 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 3 H), 0.83 (s, 9 H), 0.84 (s,
9 H), 0.95 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 3 H), 1.07 (d, J = 7.1 Hz, 3 H), 1.28 and 1.35
(2 s, 6 H), 1.68-1.78 (m, 2 H), 2.05 (dq, J = 7.0, 4.1 Hz, 1 H), 2.64
(ddc, J = 7.0, 2.1 Hz, 1 H), 3.44 (dd, J = 11.3 Hz, 1 H), 3.63 (dd, J =
11.4, 5.2 Hz, 1 H), 3.63-3.66 (m, 1 H), 3.68 (dd, J = 6.9, 4.0 Hz, 1 H),
3.88 (dd, J = 8.5, 2.2 Hz, 1 H), 9.78 (d, J = 2.0 Hz, 1 H); 13C NMR (100
MHz, CDCl3): δ = -4.6, -3.7, -3.4, -3.3, 9.6, 12.3, 12.5, 12.8, 18.2,
18.4, 19.5, 26.0, 29.6, 30.3, 39.3, 43.9, 50.5, 66.1, 74.2, 74.9, 76.1,
97.8, 204.9.
