$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Hydroxy aldehyde (+)-94-2: To a stirred solution of diol (+)-94-1 (8 mg,
0.01 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (0.6 mL) at 25°C were added PhI(OAc)2 (10 mg, 0.03
mmol) and TEMPO (1.6 mg, 0.01 mmol). The reaction mixture was stirred at
25°C for 24 h and then sequentially quenched with saturated aqueous
solutions of Na2S2O3 (1 mL) and NaHCO3 (1 mL). The resulting mixture was
extracted with Et2O (2 × 5 mL), dried (MgSO4), and concentrated under
reduced pressure. The crude residue was purified by flash column
chromatography (silica, EtOAc/hexanes, 6%) to afford hydroxyl aldehyde
(+)-94-2 (7 mg, 88%) as an oil. compound (+)-94-2, yield (7 mg, 88%) Rf =
0.38 (silica, EtOAc:hexanes, 1:6); [α]25 D = +110.8 (c = 0.6, CHCl3); IR
νmax (film): 3696brs, 2946m, 1696w, 1458w, 1370w, 1244w, 1057s cm-1; 1H
NMR (C6D6, 600 MHz): δ = 10.54 (s, 1 H), 5.63 (s, 1 H), 5.14 (d, J = 4.8
Hz, 1 H), 4.88 (d, J = 4.8 Hz, 1 H), 4.87 (s, 1 H), 4.76 (s, 1 H), 4.56
(s, 1 H), 4.47 (s, 1 H), 4.31 (s, 1 H), 3.99 (m, 1 H), 3.85 (s, 1 H),
3.80 (m, 1 H), 2.76 (dt, J = 7.8, 7.8 Hz, 1 H), 2.62 (t, J = 8.4 Hz, 1
H), 2.42 (dt, J = 11.4, 7.8 Hz, 1 H), 2.20 - 2.05 (m, 4 H), 2.04 (m, 2
H), 1.97 (m, 2 H), 1.84 (m, H), 1.72 (m, 2 H), 1.60 (s, 3 H), 1.57 (s, 3
H), 1.52 (m, 2 H), 1.50 (s, 3 H), 1.49 - 1.36 (m, 5 H), 1.28 (s, 3 H),
1.20 (t, J = 11.4 Hz, 1 H), 1.12 (s, 3 H), 1.09 (m, 1 H), 1.06 (t, J =
7.8 Hz, 9 H), 0.75 (m, 6 H), 0.05 (s, 9 H) ppm; 13C NMR (C6D6, 150 MHz):
δ = 201.83, 150.53, 143.91, 115.27, 112.25, 98.00, 97.48, 81.48, 74.06,
73.21, 72.22, 71.07, 66.32, 64.30, 57.87, 56.69, 52.57, 51.49, 49.76,
48.16, 44.83, 44.38, 37.20, 32.26, 30.25, 29.72, 29.54, 28.98, 28.65,
25.58, 24.87, 23.65, 22.63, 22.30, 22.01, 18.53, 7.48, 5.84, -1.27 ppm;
HRMS calcd for C45H76O7Si2Na+ [M + Na+] 807.5020 found 807.5031.
