$DATUM N-(((2R,3S,5S,6S)-6-((3E,5E)-4,5-dimethyl-7-oxohepta-3,5-dienyl)-3-hydroxy-5-methyltetrahydr
o-2H-pyran-2-yl)methyl)acetamide (2) To a solution of 20 (3.50 mg, 0.0107
mmol) and 2,2,6,6-tetramethylpiperidine 1-oxyl (TEMPO, 0.84 mg, 0.00538
mmol) in dichloromethane (0.2 mL) was added a solution of
(diacetoxyiodo)benzene [PhI(OAc)2, 5.20 mg, 0.0161 mmol] in
dichloromethane (0.4 mL) at room temperature. The reaction mixture was
stirred for 2 h and then concentrated in vacuum. The residue was purified
on silica gel column (2 % methanol / dichloromethane) to give the pure
product as pale yellow gum (3.04 mg, 87 %). [α]20 D -14.5° (c 0.30,
methanol ); HRMS-ESI (m/z): [M+Na+]: calcd: 346.1994, found: 346.1997; IR
(neat) 3367, 2927, 2857, 1652, 1428, 1377, 1156, 1107, 1067 cm-1; 1H NMR
(500 MHz, CD3OD, δ) 10.08 (d, J = 7.9 Hz, 1H), 6.22 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 1H),
6.03 (d, J = 7.9 Hz, 1H), 3.53 (dd, J = 14.1, 2.6 Hz, 1H), 3.44-3.35 (m,
2H), 3.35-3.30 (m, 1H), 3.06 (ddd, J = 9.6, 7.0, 2.7 Hz, 1H), 2.40-2.33
(m, 1H), 2.31 (s, 3H), 1.94 (s, 3H), 1.90 (ddd, J = 12.5, 4.8, 2.5 Hz,
1H), 1.85 (s, 3H), 1.85-1.80 (m, 1H), 1.63-1.57 (m, 2H), 1.49-1.39 (m,
1H), 0.95 (d, J = 7.1 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CD3OD, δ) 194.3, 173.8,
160.9, 137.3, 136.8, 126.2, 83.1, 80.3, 65.0, 42.5, 40.8, 34.2, 33.2,
26.9, 22.4, 14.5, 14.0, 13.0.
