$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Oxidation of Alcohols to the Corresponding
Aldehydes and Ketones (Table 1, Entries 1-6) Reagent 3 (0.5 g, 0.65 mmol)
was added to a solution of alcohol (0.5 mmol) and TEMPO (9.4 mg, 0.06
mmol) in acetone (3 mL) and the mixture was stirred at r.t. for 2 h. The
reaction mixture was then filtered to remove the polymer, which was
washed with Et2O (5 mL). The filtrate was poured into H2O (10 mL), and
extracted with Et2O (3 × 10 mL). The combined organic layers were dried
over Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. The pure product was
obtained by filtration of the crude product through silica gel. Table 1,
entry 3, yield 88%.
