$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Aldehyde (-)-21: To a stirred solution of hydroxy carbonate (-)-19-1 (430
mg, 0.435 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (25 mL) at 25 °C was added PhI(OAc)2 (2.0
equiv, 0.28 g, 0.87 mmol) and TEMPO (1.0 equiv, 66 mg, 0.435 mmol). The
resulting mixture was stirred for 24 h and then quenched with a mixture
of saturated aqueous NaHCO3 solution (5 mL) and saturated aqueous Na2S2O3
(5 mL). The resulting mixture was extracted with Et2O (2 x 15 mL), dried
(MgSO4), and concentrated in vacuo. The crude residue was purified by
flash column chromatography (silica, EtOAc/hexanes, 2 - 10%) to furnish
aldehyde carbonate (-)-21as a white foam, yield 370 mg, 0.375 mmol, 87%.
Rf = 0.40 (silica, Et2O:hexanes, 4:6); [α]25D = -36.67 (c = 0.6, CHCl3);
IR (film): νmax = 2952s, 2891s, 1749s, 1716m, 1438w, 1374m, 1267m, 1039s
cm-1; 1H NMR (C6D6, 600 MHz): δ = 9.86 (s, 1 H), 7.42 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 2
H), 7.36 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 2 H), 7.19 - 7.16 (m, 4 H), 7.10 - 7.05 (m, 2
H), 6.00 (s, 1 H), 5.71 (s, 1 H), 4.98 (s, 1 H), 4.93 (s, 1 H), 4.85 (d,
J = 7.8 Hz, 1 H), 4.82 - 4.78 (m, 2 H), 4.73 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 1 H), 4.67
(d, J = 7.2 Hz, 1 H), 4.60 (d, J = 9.6 Hz, 1 H), 4.57 (d, J = 9.6 Hz, 1
H), 4.53 (m, 3 H), 4.47 (d, J = 6.0 Hz, 1 H), 4.41 (d, J = 12.0 Hz, 1 H),
4.33 (d, J = 6.6 Hz, 1 H), 4.22 (s, 1 H), 4.02 (d, J = 11.4 Hz, 1 H),
3.94 (m, 1 H), 3.77 (d, J = 11.4 Hz, 1 H), 3.68 (m, 1 H), 3.32 (s, 3 H),
2.96 (t, J = 7.8 Hz, 1 H), 2.82 (ddd, J = 10.2, 7.8, 4.2 Hz, 1 H), 2.70
