$DATUM Aldehyde 7 To a solution of S1 (255 mg, 0.550 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (5 mL) were
added TEMPO (16.7 mg, 0.109 mmol) and PhI(OAc)2 (213 mg, 0.661 mmol) at
room temperature under an Ar atmosphere. The mixture was stirred for 23 h
and then concentrated in vacuo. The residue was purified by silica gel
column chromatography (AcOEt:hexane = 1:99, then 2:98) to give aldehyde 7
(221 mg, 0.478 mmol, 87%) as a colorless oil. [α]D 27 +22.9 (c 1.07,
CHCl3); 1H-NMR (CDCl3) δ 0.60 (6H, q, J = 7.8 Hz), 0.94 (9H, t, J = 7.8
Hz), 1.94 – 2.04 (2H, m), 2.08 – 2.17 (2H, m), 2.63 – 2.80 (2H, m), 3.44
(1H, dd, J = 5.6, 9.6 Hz), 3.62 (1H, dd, J = 5.6, 9.6 Hz), 3.80 (3H, s),
3.92 (1H, dt, J = 2.4, 5.6 Hz), 4.22 (1H, tt, J = 3.4, 9.7 Hz), 4.36 (1H,
td, J = 2.4, 11.2 Hz), 4.45 (1H, d, J = 15.8 Hz), 4.48 (1H, d, J = 15.8
Hz), 6.88 (2H, d, J = 8.7 Hz), 7.25 (2H, d, J = 8.7 Hz),9.82 (1H, s);
13C-NMR (CDCl3) δ 5.0, 6.8, 30.9, 41.0, 43.0, 55.2, 60.0, 61.2, 71.2,
73.0, 73.3, 113.6, 129.2, 129.9, 159.0, 200.6; IR (neat) 2955, 2912,
2875, 2724, 1726, 1613, 1586, 1513, 1462, 1414, 1363, 1301, 1247, 1173,
1096, 1035, 1007, 975, 820, 781, 743; FAB-MS m/z 485 (M++Na);
High-Resolution FAB-MS m/z 485.1677 (M++Na, calcd for C22H33Cl2O4SiNa
485.1658).
