$DATUM Hydroxy aldehyde (+)-111 and Acetoxy aldehyde (+)-112: To a stirred
solution of diol (+)-110 (143 mg, 0.142 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (4 mL) at 25 °C
were added PhI(OAc)2 (2.0 equiv, 91 mg, 0.284 mmol) and 1-Me-AZADO (0.2
equiv, 5 mg, 0.028 mmol). The reaction mixture was stirred at 25 °C for
18 h and then quenched with saturated aqueous solutions of Na2S2O3 (2 mL)
and NaHCO3 (2 mL). The resulting mixture was extracted with Et2O (2 x 10
mL), dried (MgSO4), and concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude
residue was purified by flash column chromatography (silica,
EtOAc/hexanes, 5 - 15% aldehyde (+)-111. To a solution of this
intermediate in CH2Cl2 (3 mL) at 25 °C were added Et3N (20 equiv, 0.40
mL, 2.84 mmol), 4-DMAP (1.0 equiv, 17 mg, 0.142 mmol), and Ac2O (10
equiv, 0.13 mL, 1.42 mmol). The reaction mixture was stirred for 18 h at
25 °C and then quenched with saturated aqueous NaHCO3 solution (20 mL).
The resulting mixture was , dried (MgSO4), and concentrated under reduced
pressure. The crude residue was purified by flash column chromatography
(silica, EtOAc/hexanes, 2 - 15%) to afford acetoxy aldehyde (+)-112 as an
oil, yield 129 mg, 0.124 mmol, 87% for two steps. Rf = 0.30 (silica,
EtOAc:hexanes, 1:9); [α]25D = +40.2 (c = 0.5, CHCl3); IR (film): νmax =
2952s, 2876s, 1738s, 1699s, 1460w, 1371m, 1246m, 1051s cm-1; 1H NMR
(C6D6, 500 MHz): δ = 10.53 (s, 1 H), 5.59 (s, 1 H), 5.50 (t, J = 3.0 Hz,
1 H), 5.20 (d, J = 6.0 Hz, 1 H), 5.01 (d, J = 6.0 Hz, 1 H), 4.89 (s, 1
H), 4.82 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1 H), 4.80 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1 H), 4.79 (m, 1 H),
4.79 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 1 H), 4.78 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 1 H), 4.55 (s, 1 H), 4.48
(d, J = 4.5 Hz, 1 H), 4.11 (d, J = 1.5 Hz, 1 H), 3.89 - 3.83 (m, 2 H),
3.77 - 3.72 (m, 3 H), 3.56 (m, 1 H), 3.02 (d, J = 4.0 Hz, 1 H), 2.55 -
2.59 (m, 2 H), 2.41 (dt, J = 9.0, 7.5 Hz, 1 H), 2.27 (ddd, J = 11.5, 8.0,
4.5 Hz, 1 H), 2.22 - 2.14 (m, 2 H), 2.10 - 2.04 (m, 2 H), 1.92 - 1.81 (m,
2 H), 1.80 (s, 3 H), 1.75 (m, 1 H), 1.72 (m, 1 H), 1.71 (s, 3 H), 1.69 -
1.66 (m, 2 H), 1.63 - 1.59 (m, 2 H), 1.52 (ddd, J = 13.0, 8.5, 4.5 Hz, 1
H), 1.34 (m, 4 H), 1.29 (s, 3 H), 1.26 (s, 3 H), 1.19 (t, J = 11.0 Hz, 1
H), 1.05 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 9 H), 1.00 (m, 7 H), 0.73 (dq, J = 8.0, 4.0 Hz,
6 H), 0.06 (s, 9 H), 0.02 (s, 9 H), 0.00 (s, 9 H) ppm; 13C NMR (C6D6, 125
MHz): δ = 200.15, 169.53, 150.08, 143.92, 118.70, 111.38, 96.53, 94.95,
89.50, 87.74, 81.26, 77.50, 76.28, 71.67, 67.15, 66.56, 66.47, 65.18,
59.55, 59.20, 58.45, 51.58, 51.11, 50.42, 49.47, 43.64, 41.60, 32.55,
30.01, 28.44, 26.87, 26.28, 26.10, 24.03, 23.71, 23.35, 23.25, 20.81,
18.70, 18.60, 7.68, 6.23, -0.96, -1.13 ppm; HRMS calcd for
C56H102O10Si4Na+ [M + Na+] 1069.6442 found 1069.6452.
