$DATUM Aldehyde 37: To a stirred solution of alcohol 36 (15.3 mg, 28.8 μmol) in
CH2Cl2 (0.3 mL) were added iodobenzen diacetate (17.2 mg, 53.4 μmol) and
TEMPO (1.0 mg, 6.4 μmol) at room temperature. The mixture was stirred at
room temperature for 5 h, diluted with saturated aqueous Na2S2O3 (3 mL),
and extracted with EtOAc (3 × 5 mL). The combined extracts were washed
with saturated aqueous NaHCO3 (3 mL) and brine (3 mL), dried (Na2SO4),
filtered, and concentrated. The residual oil was purified by column
chromatography on silica gel (12 g, hexane-EtOAc 8:1 to 4:1). Yield:
(13.2 mg, 87%), colorless oil. [α]D23 +10.5° (c 1.40, CHCl3) IR (neat,
cm-1) 2953, 2925, 2727, 1725, 1615, 1518, 1341, 1249, 1171, 1096, 1060,
1034, 829; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 9.85 (dd, J= 2.0, 1.8 Hz, 1H), 7.40
(d, J= 8.6 Hz, 2H), 6.89 (d, J= 8.6 Hz, 2H), 6.45 (dt, J= 14.4, 7.4 Hz,
1H), 5.96 (dt, J= 14.4, 1.4 Hz, 1H), 5.50 (s, 1H), 5.17 (dq, J= 10.6, 1.1
Hz, 1H), 4.47 (m, 1H), 3.81 (m, 1H), 3.81 (s, 3H), 3.72 (dd, J= 8.5, 6.3
Hz, 1H), 3.15 (s, 3H), 2.79 (ddd, J= 16.8, 7.4, 2.0 Hz, 1H), 2.61 (ddd,
J= 16.8, 5.2, 1.8 Hz, 1H), 2.56 (m, 1H), 2.09 (m, 1H), 2.03-1.92 (m, 2H),
1.70 (ddd, J= 12.8, 2.5, 2.2 Hz, 1H), 1.65 (m, 1H), 1.55 (d, J=1.1 Hz,
3H), 1.52 (dt, J= 12.8, 11.0 Hz, 1H), 0.99 (d, J= 6.7 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 200.7, 160.0, 145.2, 135.0, 133.0, 131.0, 127.4,
113.7, 100.6, 83.3, 75.7, 73.6, 71.9, 55.7, 55.4, 49.5, 43.6, 39.3, 36.7,
32.0, 21.0, 10.6; HRMS (ESI) m/z 529.1476, calcd for C24H34IO5 [M+H]+
529.1451.
