$DATUM Methyl (2S, 3R, 4S, 5S)-3,
5-bis-(t-Butyldimethylsilyloxy)-7-oxo-2,4-dimethyl heptanoate (30)
Alcohol 29 (460 mg, 1.025 mmol) was dissolved in DCM (5 mL). PhI(OAc)2
(528 mg, 1.64 mmol) was added, followed by TEMPO (32 mg, 0.205 mmol), and
the reaction mixture was stirred at RT for 4 h. Aq. Na2S2O3 (10 mL) was
added, and the mixture was vigorously stirred for a further 20 min,
before being extracted with DCM (3 x 10 mL). The combined organic
extracts were dried (Na2SO4), concentrated under reduced pressure, and
purified by flash chromatography (10% Et2O in hexane), to afford aldehyde
30 as a colorless oil (395 mg, 86%). Methyl (2S, 3R, 4S, 5S)-3,
5-bis-(t-Butyldimethylsilyloxy)-7-oxo-2,4-dimethyl heptanoate (30), Yield
395 mg, 86% Rf0.61 (33% AcOEt in hexane); [α]D 20-18.4 (c 0.85, CHCl3);
IR (thin film) 2954 (s), 2930 (s), 2858 (s), 1731 (s, C=O), 1473 (s),
1253 (s), 1082 (s), 836 (s), 775 (s); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δH 9.80
(1H, s, CHO), 4.60 - 4.56 (1H, m, H5), 4.02 (1H, dd, J = 8.2, 2.6 Hz,
H3), 3.68 (3H, s, OMe), 2.64 (1H, dq, J = 7.1, 2.6 Hz, H2), 2.50 (1H,
ddd, J = 15.6, 9.1, 3.1 Hz, H6A), 2.49 - 2.43 (1H, m, H6B), 1.92 - 1.87
(1H, m, H4), 1.15 (3H, d, J = 7.1 Hz, Me2), 0.90 - 0.85 (21H, m, Me4 + 2
x SiC(Me)3), 0.07 (3H, s, SiMe), 0.05 (3H, s, SiMe), 0.04 (3H, s, SiMe),
-0.05 (3H, s, SiMe); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δC 202.4, 175.3, 74.3,
67.6, 51.7, 45.7, 43.7, 42.7, 26.1, 25.7, 18.3, 17.9, 10.4, 9.7, -4.1,
-4.2, -4.3, -4.7; m/z (CI+) 469.28 (100, [M+Na]+); HRMS (+ESI) calcd for
C22H46O5Si2Na [M+Na]+ 469.2782, found 469.2780.
