$DATUM (S)-2-(tert-butyldiphenylsilyloxy)tetradecanal (12). To a solution of 11
(106 mg, 0.227 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (4 mL) was added BAIB (84 mg, 0.261 mmol)
and a catalytic amount of TEMPO. The reaction mixture was stirred at room
temperature for 6 hours. Evaporation gave a residue, which was dissolved
in tBuOMe (5 mL) and washed with a 10% aq. solution of Na2S2O3 (3 × 5
mL), and an aq. satured NaHCO3 solution (3 × 5 mL). After drying with
Na2SO4 and solvent evaporated under reduced pressure, the residue was
purified by chromatography on silica-gel (1% EtOAc/Hexane) affording
compound. Yield: 91 mg (86%); orange oil. [α]D22 =-3.8 (c 1.0, CHCl3; Rf
= 0.83 (10% EtOAc/Hexane); IR (NaCl, neat): 2954, 2926, 2855, 1736 cm-1;
1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 9.63 (s, 1H, H-1); 7.66(m, 4H, CHo-Ph); 7.44
(m, 6H, CHm,p-Ph); 4.08 (t, 1H, J = 5.8Hz, H-2); 1.65 (m, 2H, H-3); 1.31
(s, 20H, H-4 to H-13); 1.17 (s, 9H, tBu-TBDPS); 0.93 (t, 3H, J = 6.8Hz,
H-14); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 204.04 (CH-1); 135.86 (CHo-Ph);
133.26(C-Ph); 130.04 (CHm-Ph); 127.83 (CHp-Ph); 78.10 (CH-2); 32.92-29.42
(5CH2); 27.00 (CH3-tBu-TBDPS); 24.09(CH2); 22.75 (CH2); 19.41
(C-tBu-TBDPS); 14.19 (CH3); MS (ESI+): m/z (%) = 489.31 ([M + Na] +,31),
467.33 ([M + 1] +, 86), 403.25 (60), 389.28 (35); HRMS (ESI+): m/z calcd
for C25H48NaO6, 467.3343; found, 467.3339.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of (+)-muricatacin and a formal synthesis of CMI-977 from
