$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for oxidation of alcohols to
aldehydes: To an oven-dried roundbottom flask containing a 23 °C solution
of the appropriate alcohol (1.0 equiv) and CH2Cl2 (0.5 M) was added
iodobenzene diacetate (1.05 equiv) and TEMPO (0.1 equiv). The solution
stirred for 14 h. and was quenched by the addition of 1.0 M Na2S2O3
aqueous solution. After 10 minutes of vigorous stirring, the aqueous
layer was extracted with CH2Cl2 (2x). The combined organic layers were
washed with saturated NaHCO3 (1x), brine (1x) and were dried with Na2SO4,
filtered, and concentrated. Purification by flash column chromatography
afforded the desired aldehyde. 6-(triisopropylsilyl)hex-5-yn-1-ol:
Prepared following the general procedure from the known alcohol.9
6-(triisopropylsilyl)hex-5-ynal (2.32 g, 9.12 mmol), iodobenzene
diacetate (2.94 g, 9.12 mmol), TEMPO (142 mg, 0.912 mmol) and
dichloromethane (18.2 mL). Purification by flash column chromatography
using 5% ether in pentanes afforded 6-(triisopropylsilyl)hex-5-yn-1-ol
(1.95 g, 7.72 mmol, 85% yield). IR (thin film, cm-1) ν 2942, 2891, 2865,
2717, 2171, 1727, 1463, 1383, 1365, 1327, 1242, 1072, 1015, 995, 919,
882, 674, 659 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 9.82 (m, 1H), 2.63 (td, J = 7.3,
1.4 Hz, 2H), 2.34 (t, J = 6.8 Hz, 2H), 1.85 (p, J = 7.0 Hz, 2H), 1.05 (m,
21H). 13C NMR (126 MHz, CDCl3) δ 202.03, 107.45, 81.54, 42.74, 21.24,
19.27, 18.65, 11.25. HRMS (ESI-TOF) Calculated for C15H28OSi [M+H]:
253.19877 Found: 253.19817
