$DATUM (2S,3S)-2-Azido-1,3-di(benzyloxy)octadecan-4-one (18) A mixture of
alcohol 17 (640 mg, 1.02 mmol), PhI(OAc)2 (803 mg, 2.44 mmol) and TEMPO
(38.2 mg, 0.244 mmol) in DCM (6.1 mL) was stirred at r.t. for 48 h.
Concentration in vacuo and purification by column chromatography
(acetone/petroleum ether 0→5%) afforded ketone 18 as a colourless oil
(540 mg, 85%). [α]D -5.8 (c 1.13, CHCl3); IR (cm-1) 2923 vs, 2853 s, 2099
s, 1717 m, 1455 m, 1101 m; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) 7.40-7.30 (10H, m),
4.62 (1H, d, J = 11.5 Hz), 4.57 (1H, d, J = 11.5 Hz), 4.53 (2H, s),
3.97-3.91 (2H, m), 3.72 (1H, dd, J = 10.0, 4.5 Hz), 3.66 (1H, dd, J =
10.0, 6.5 Hz), 2.57 (1H, dt, J = 18.0, 7.0 Hz), 2.51 (1H, dt, J = 18.0,
7.0 Hz), 1.55-1.49 (2H, m), 1.35-1.21 (22H, m), 0.90 (3H, t, J = 7.0 Hz);
13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) 210.2, 137.7, 137.0, 128.7, 128.6, 128.3, 128.2,
128.0, 127.8, 83.5, 73.6, 68.8, 62.2, 39.6, 32.1, 29.82, 29.76, 29.62,
29.57, 29.50, 29.3, 23.1, 22.8, 14.3; ES+ m/z (%) 544 ((M+Na)+, 100);
HRMS (ES+) for C32H47N3O3 (M+Na)+: Calcd 544.3510; Measured 544.3511.
