$DATUM 5,8,8-Trimethyl-3,4,8,9-tetrahydro-1H-cyclopenta[h]isochromen-7-one (22)
To a solution of (+)-3 (44 mg, 0.19 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (1 mL) were added
TEMPO (3 mg, 0.02 mmol, 10 mol%) and diacetoxy iodobenzene (DIB) (67 mg,
0.21 mmol). The reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature for 9 h.
After dilution with CH2Cl2 (5 mL), the mixture was washed with a
saturated aqueous solution of Na2S2O3 (5 mL) and extracted with CH2Cl2 (3
x 5 mL). The combined organic layers were washed with a saturated aqueous
solution of NaHCO3 (5 mL) and brine, dried with MgSO4, filtered and
concentrated. Purification of the residual oil by flash chromatography
(95:5 heptane/EtOAc) afforded 22 (37 mg, 0.16 mmol, 85% yield) as a white
solid;
5,8,8-Trimethyl-3,4,8,9-tetrahydro-1H-cyclopenta[h]isochromen-7-one (22),
yield (37 mg, 0.16 mmol, 85%). Rf 0.43 (60:40 heptane/EtOAc), mp 81-82
°C. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.22 (s, 6H), 2.29 (s, 3H), 2.73 (s, 2H),
2.78 (t, J = 5.8 Hz, 2H), 4.04 (t, J = 5.8 Hz, 2H), 4.75 (s, 2H), 7.46
(s, 1H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 19.1 (q), 25.6 (q), 27.1 (t), 40.3
(t), 45.7 (s), 65.0 (t), 65.8 (t), 122.9 (d), 132.3 (s), 133.0 (s), 136.5
(s), 139.5 (s), 145.9 (s), 211.0 (s); IR (neat): νmax/cm-1 = 1703, 1601,
1433, 1312, 1120, 779; MS [ESI (+)]: m/z (%) = 231 (100), 213 (13), 201
(22), 183 (72), 168 (15); HRMS [ESI (+)]: Mass calcd for [C15H19O2]+,
231.1385; found, 231.1376.
