$DATUM (R)-2-Methyl-3-(oxazol-4-yl)propanal, 46.
(R)-2-Methyl-3-(oxazol-4-yl)propan-1-ol (2.33 mg, 16.51 mmol) was
dissolved in anhydrous DCM (80 mL), and treated successively with
(diacetoxyiodo)benzene (7.45 g, 23.1 mmol) and TEMPO (258 mg, 1.65 mmol).
The reaction mixture was then stirred under argon at room temperature
until completion as indicated by TLC analysis (16 h). The reaction
mixture was diluted with DCM (150 mL), washed with sat'd aqueous sodium
thiosulfate solution (2 x 60 mL), water (2 x 30 mL) and brine (30 mL).
The phases were separated and the organic layer was dried over anhydrous
sodium sulfate and then concentrated under reduced pressure to afford the
crude product as an orange oil. Purification of the crude residue by
flash column chromatography (silica gel, elution gradient 0 - 20 % ethyl
acetate in hexanes) afforded (R)-2-methyl-3-(oxazol-4-yl)propanal, 46
(1.93 g, 13.87 mmol, 84%) as a colourless oil.
(R)-2-Methyl-3-(oxazol-4-yl)propanal, 46, yield (1.93 g, 13.87 mmol, 84%)
1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ: 1.13 (1H, d, J = 6.8 Hz), 2.61 (1H, dd, J =
14.8, 6.9 Hz), 2.76 - 2.86 (1H, m), 2.97 (1H, ddd, J = 14.8, 6.5, 0.5
Hz), 7.45 (1H, br. d, J = 1.0 Hz), 7.82 (1H, s), 9.73 (1H, d, J = 1.3
Hz). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 125 MHz) δ: 13.4, 26.9, 45.5, 135.5, 137.5, 151.2,
204.1. m/z [Cl+ (+ve), isobutane] 140 [M+H]+ (100%). HRMS found [M+H]+
140.0711, C7H10NO2 requires 140.0712. υmax / cm-1 (film): 3137, 2974,
2936, 1724, 1516. [α]D +41.70 (c = 0.93, CHCl3).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Regiocontrolled Rearrangement of Isobenzofurans
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Egan, Ben A.; Paradowski, Michael; Thomas, Lynne H.; Marquez, Rodolfo
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2011), 13(8), 2086-2089

