$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: To a solution of diol 54 (95.6 mg, 0.508 mmol)
in CH2Cl2 (2.5 mL) and pH 7 phosphate buffer (2.5 mL) were added
PhI(OAc)2 (986 mg) and AZADO (4.3 mg, 0.028 mmol) at 0 °C. The resultant
mixture was gradually warmed to room temperature, stirred for 19 h and
then quenched with saturated aqueous Na2S2O3. The resulting solution was
extracted with EtOAc (3 times). The organic layer was washed with brine,
dried over MgSO4 and filtered. The solution was concentrated and the
residue was purified with flash column chromatography (EtOAc/hexane =
1/9) to afford carboxylic acid 7a. 7b (63.4 mg, 0.317 mmol, 84% from 71.3
mg, 0.379 mmol of 54b). [α]D20 = -24 (c = 0.42, CHCl3)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM buffered solution (phosphate) used in stage 1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Total Synthesis and Complete Structural Assignment of Yaku'amide A
