$DATUM (2S, 3R, 4S, 5S)-3, 5,
7-tris-(t-Butyldimethylsilyloxy)-2,4-dimethylheptan-1-al (26) Alcohol 25
(3.04 g, 5.68 mmol) was dissolved in DCM (100 mL). PhI(OAc)2 (5.49 g,
17.04 mmol) was added, followed by TEMPO (177 mg, 1.136 mmol), and the
reaction mixture was stirred at RT for 2 h. Aq. Na2S2O3 (100 mL) was
added, and the mixture was vigorously stirred for a further 20 min,
before being extracted with DCM (3 x 50 mL). The combined organic
extracts were dried (Na2SO4), concentrated under reduced pressure, and
purified by flash chromatography (10% Et2O in hexane), to afford the
desired aldehyde 26 as a colorless oil (2.51 g, 83%). (2S, 3R, 4S, 5S)-3,
5, 7-tris-(t-Butyldimethylsilyloxy)-2,4-dimethylheptan-1-al (26), Yield
2.51 g, 83% Rf0.70 (33% AcOEt in hexane); [α]D 20-31.0 (c 1, CHCl3); IR
(thin film) 2955 (s), 2930 (s), 2858 (s), 1729 (s, C=O), 1472 (s), 1253
(s), 1086 (s), 832 (s), 772 (s); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δH 9.71 (1H, s,
CHO), 4.20 (1H, dd, J = 7.9, 1.9 Hz, H3), 3.99 (1H, ddd, J = 8.2, 8.1,
4.3 Hz, H5), 3.77 - 3.71 (1H, m, H7A), 3.66 - 3.61 (1H, m, H7B), 2.51
(1H, dq, J = 7.0, 1.8 Hz, H2), 1.90 - 1.85 (1H, m, H4), 1.70 - 1.62 (2H,
m, H6A + H6B), 1.13 (3H, d, J = 7.0 Hz, Me2), 0.91 - 0.85 (30H, m, Me4 +
3 x SiC(Me)3), 0.05 - 0.03 (12H, m, 2 x Si(Me)2), -0.03 (3H, s, SiMe);
13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δC 205.1, 71.8, 69.2, 60.8, 50.4, 43.8, 34.8,
26.1, 26.0, 25.8, 18.4, 18.3, 18.0, 10.6, 7.3, -3.9, -4.1, -4.3, -4.5,
-5.28, -5.30; m/z (+ESI) 555.37 (100, [M+Na]+); HRMS (+ESI) calcd for
C27H60O4Si3Na [M+Na]+ 555.3699, found 555.3697.
