$DATUM (E)-methyl 4-(4-methoxybenzyloxy)-3-(3-oxopropoxy)but-2-enoate (13). To a
solution of alcohol 12 (1.89 g, 6.09 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (8 mL) was added
PhI(OAc)2 (2.35 g, 7.31 mmol) and TEMPO (95 mg, 0.61 mmol) and the
mixture was stirred at room temperature for 2 h. After removal of the
solvent in vacuo the remaining residue was purified by column
chromatography (EtOAc:petrol 1:2). Aldehyde 13 as a colourless oil, yield
1.52 g, 81%. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 2.91 (td, J = 6.1, 1.2 Hz, 2H),
3.69 (s, 3H), 3.80 (s, 3H), 4.12 (t, J = 6.1 Hz, 2H), 4.48 (s, 2H), 4.61
(s, 2H), 5.17 (s, 1H), 6.87 (d, J = 8.7 Hz, 2H), 7.26 (d, J = 8.7 Hz,
2H), 9.81 (t, J = 1.2 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 42.3, 51.0,
55.1, 61.8, 66.2, 72.6, 93.9, 113.6, 129.4, 130.0, 159.1, 166.9, 169.7,
198.8; IR (film) νmax: 2952, 1714, 1612, 1513, 1245, 1142, 1076, 1031
cm-1; HRMS (ESI) calcd for C16H20O6Na ([M+Na]+) 331.1152; found 331.1152.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Ketyl Radical Cyclization of β-Disubstituted Acrylates: Formal Syntheses
