$DATUM Compound 22. A solution of 21 (0.0458 g, 0.0720 mmol) and iodobenzene
diacetate (0.118 g, 0.366 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (2.0 mL) was treated with TEMPO
(1.0 mg, 0.0064 mmol) at room temperature. After 2 h, the reaction
mixture was concentrated to approximately 1 mL and purified by silica gel
chromatography (4:1-2:1 hex:EtOAc) to provide 22 (0.0370 g, 81%) as a
white foam. [α]22D -82.1° (c 0.42, CH2Cl2); IR (thin film) 3421, 2954,
2876, 1740, 1695, 1652, 1456, 1380, 1242, 1182, 1158, 1107, 1070, 1012
cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 9.58 (t, J = 2.2 Hz, 1H), 6.95 (s, 1H),
6.54 (s, 1H), 5.32 (dd, J = 5.9, 10.0 Hz, 1H), 5.09 (d, J = 9.9 Hz, 1H),
4.07 (t, J = 6.4 Hz, 1H), 3.83 (s br, 1H), 3.12 (dd, J = 2.2, 15.9 Hz,
1H), 3.05-3.02 (m, 1H), 2.94 (d, J = 15.6 Hz, 1H), 2.91-2.85 (m, 1H),
2.81-2.69 (m, 5H), 2.55-2.43 (m, 1H), 2.18 (dd, J = 5.5, 14.0 Hz, 1H),
2.10 (s, 3H), 1.96-1.87 (m, 1H), 1.79-1.60 (m, 2H), 1.42-1.33 (m, 1H),
1.28-1.22 (m, 2H), 1.15 (s, 3H), 1.13-1.11 (m, 6H), 0.87 (t, J = 7.9 Hz,
9H), 0.60-0.48 (m, 6H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 217.9, 200.1, 170.6,
164.7, 152.3, 137.8, 134.8, 125.9, 120.0, 116.3, 78.9, 75.7, 73.6, 53.6,
50.6, 43.3, 39.5, 38.4, 32.5, 30.2, 29.6, 25.9, 24.0, 22.6, 19.2, 16.7,
15.2, 14.1, 7.0, 5.2; HRMS (EI+ ) calcd for C34H55NO6SSi (M + H)+
634.3598, found 634.3606.
