$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Oxidation of
Propargyl Alcohols to Propargyl Aldehydes. To the solution of TEMPO (269
mg, 1.7 mmol) and alcohol (17.6 mmol) in DCM (17.7 mL) was added
bisacetoxyiodobenzene (6.28 g, 19.5 mmol). The reaction mixture was
stirred for 1.5 h. Then the organic layer was washed with aqueous
solution of Na2S2O3. The water layer was extracted with methylene
chloride, and then combined organic extracts were washed with aqueous
solution of NaHCO3 to pH 7, dried (Na2SO4), filtered, and evaporated.
(4-Nitrophenyl)propynal as colorless crystals, yield 2.16 g, 81%. mp =
120.2-120.7 °C (CH2Cl2/hexane) [mp = 123.0-123.5 °C(petroleum ether)];
1HNMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.78 (m, 2H), 8.28 (m, 2H), 9.47 (s, 1H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Dess-Martin oxidation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of trans-A2B2-Porphyrins Bearing Phenylethynyl Substituents
