$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Aldehyde 38: (Diacetoxyiodo)benzene (BAIB) (1.97 g, 6.11 mmol) was added
to a solution of alcohol 37 (2.05 g, 5.56 mmol) and
(2,2,6,6-Tetramethylpiperidinin-1-yl)oxyl (TEMPO) (86.87 mg, 0.56 mmol)
in CH2Cl2 (25 mL). The reaction mixture was stirred at 23 ºC for 18 h
then was quenched with a saturated aqueous solution of NH4Cl (100 mL) and
extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 x 100 mL). The combined organic layers were
dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, filtered and concentrated. The residue was
purified by flash chromatography (Hexane/CH2Cl2 5:1 to 1:2). 38 (1.733 g,
79% yield) as a colourless oil. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz) δ: 9.72 (t, 1H, J
= 2.7 Hz), 7.74-7.67 (m, 4H), 7.48-7.37 (m, 6H), 5.56-5.45 (m, 1H),
5.32-5.23 (m, 1H), 4.29-4.20 (m, 1H), 2.51-2.48 (m, 2H), 2.31-2.27 (m,
2H), 1.43 (dd, 3H, J = 6.9, 1.5 Hz), 1.06 (s, 9H). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75
MHz) δ: 202.3, 136.1, 134.0, 130.1, 127.9, 127.4, 125.1, 69.4, 50.1,
35.1, 27.2, 19.5, 13.1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Isolation and First Total Synthesis of PM050489 and PM060184, Two New
Marine Anticancer Compounds
