$DATUM (E)-1-Benzyldimethylsilyl-1-hexen-3-one A solution of 1-hexyn-3-ol (0.78
g, 6.65 mmol) and benzyldimethylsilane (1.15 mL, 7.98 mmol) in THF (8 mL)
under Ar was treated with platinum(0) dimethylvinyldisiloxane complex
(0.12 mL, 2% soln, Aldrich) and then heated to reflux for 45 min. The
flask was then cooled to rt, the volatile organics removed under reduced
pressure, and the residue applied directly to a silica gel column (eluent
20:1, then 10:1 pet. ether: ether). 1.09 g (66%) of the desired terminal
silane together with significant mixed fractions which were discarded.
The allylic alcohol (342 mg, 1.38 mmol) was then taken up in CH2Cl2 and
treated sequentially with iodobenzene diacetate (488 mg, 1.52 mmol) and
TEMPO (21 mg, 0.14 mol). After stirring 4 h at rt, aq. sodium thiosulfate
(20 mL, 1.0M soln) was added, and the mixture extracted with CH2Cl2 (2 ×
25 mL). The organics were washed with sodium bicarbonate (10 mL) and
brine (10 mL), dried over Na2SO4, and concentrated in vacuo. Purification
on a silica gel column (eluent 40:1 pet. ether: ether). 98 mg (78%) of
the desired ketone as a colorless oil. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ
6.98-7.24 (m, 6H), 6.44 (d, J = 19.2 Hz, 1H), 2.55 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 2H),
2.20 (s, 2H), 1.64 (qt, J = 7.4, 7.4 Hz, 2H), 0.94 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 3H),
0.13 (s, 6H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 200.3, 144.2, 143.1, 138.8,
128.3, 128.1, 124.3, 41.3, 25.2, 17.5, 13.8, -3.9. IR (thin film) 2961,
1697, 1677, 1494, 1250, 1206, 1161, 996, 836 (s), 700 cm-1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
