$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (E)-1-Benzyldimethylsilyl-1-hexen-3-one A
solution of 1-hexyn-3-ol (0.78 g, 6.65 mmol) and benzyldimethylsilane
(1.15 mL, 7.98 mmol) in THF (8 mL) under Ar was treated with platinum(0)
dimethylvinyldisiloxane complex (0.12 mL, 2% soln, Aldrich) and then
heated to reflux for 45 min. The flask was then cooled to rt, the
volatile organics removed under reduced pressure, and the residue applied
directly to a silica gel column (eluent 20:1, then 10:1 pet. ether:
ether). 1.09 g (66%) of the desired terminal silane together with
significant mixed fractions which were discarded. The allylic alcohol
(342 mg, 1.38 mmol) was then taken up in CH2Cl2 and treated sequentially
with iodobenzene diacetate (488 mg, 1.52 mmol) and TEMPO (21 mg, 0.14
mol). After stirring 4 h at rt, aq. sodium thiosulfate (20 mL, 1.0M soln)
was added, and the mixture extracted with CH2Cl2 (2 × 25 mL). The
organics were washed with sodium bicarbonate (10 mL) and brine (10 mL),
dried over Na2SO4, and concentrated in vacuo. Purification on a silica
gel column (eluent 40:1 pet. ether: ether).
(Z)-1-(Benzyldimethylsilyl)-5-phenyl-1-penten-3-one The ketone was made
in 78% yield by oxidation1 of the allylic alcohol as for
(E)-1-Benzyldimethylsilyl-1-hexen-3-one below. Coupling constants are
consistent with the cis isomer.2 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.18-7.31 (m,
7H), 7.01-7.08 (m, 3H), 6.90 (d, J = 13.9 Hz, 1H), 6.34 (d, J = 13.9 Hz,
1H). IR (thin film) 3026, 2953, 1694 (s), 1494, 1374, 1245, 1096, 834
(s), 699 (s) cm-1.
