$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Hydroxy aldehyde (-)-38-1: To a solution of diol (+)-38 (130 mg, 0.165
mmol) in CH2Cl2 (10 mL) at 25 °C were added PhI(OAc)2 (10 equiv, 530 mg,
1.65 mmol) and TEMPO (2.0 equiv, 51 mg, 0.33 mmol). The reaction mixture
was stirred at 25 °C for 24 h and then quenched with saturated aqueous
solutions of Na2S2O3 (10 mL) and NaHCO3 (10 mL). The resulting mixture
was extracted with Et2O (2 x 20 mL), dried (MgSO4), and concentrated
under reduced pressure. The crude residue was purified by flash column
chromatography (silica, EtOAc/hexanes, 5 - 30%) to afford hydroxy
aldehyde (-)-38-1 as a white foam, yield 100 mg, 0.127 mmol, 77%. Rf =
0.55 (silica, Et2O:hexanes, 4:6); [α]25D = -50.0 (c = 0.4, CHCl3); IR
(film): νmax = 3524brs, 2946m, 2875s, 1702s, 1458w, 1378w, 1365m, 1224w,
1057s cm-1; 1H NMR (C6D6, 500 MHz): δ = 10.52 (s, 1 H), 5.74 (s, 1 H),
4.86 (s, 1 H), 4.77 (s, 1 H), 4.70 (d, J = 7.5 Hz, 1 H), 4.64 (d, J = 7.5
Hz, 1 H), 4.63 (s, 1 H), 4.38 (s, 1 H), 4.15 (s, 1 H), 3.83 (s, 1 H),
3.76 (m, 1 H), 3.66 (m, 1 H), 2.82 (dt, J = 9.5, 8.0 Hz, 1 H), 2.63 (d, J
= 3.5 Hz, 1 H), 2.54 (m, 1 H), 2.44 (m, 1 H), 2.12 (m, 4 H), 2.00 (m, 3
H), 1.90 - 1.59 (m, 6 H), 1.58 (s, 3 H), 1.59 - 1.50 (m, 2 H), 1.49 (s, 6
H), 1.46 - 1.31 (m, 3 H), 1.30 (s, 3 H), 1.18 (t, J = 9.5 Hz, 1 H), 1.11
(s, 3 H), 1.06 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 9 H), 0.98 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 2 H), 0.70 (q,
J = 8.0 Hz, 6 H), 0.05 (s, 9 H) ppm; 13C NMR (C6D6, 125 MHz): δ = 201.35,
151.03, 144.26, 117.73, 111.88, 98.76, 89.54, 76.48, 76.31, 74.38, 73.10,
71.06, 66.12, 65.16, 58.02, 57.40, 54.90, 52.47, 51.92, 51.56, 49.57,
43.31, 37.31, 32.92, 30.23, 28.19, 26.39, 26.28, 25.86, 25.51, 25.20,
24.36, 24.19, 23.73, 22.57, 18.31, 7.30, 5.42, -1.24 ppm; HRMS calcd for
C45H76O7Si2H+ [M + H+] 785.5202 found 785.5207.
