$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of diol 54 (95.6 mg, 0.508 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (2.5 mL) and pH
7 phosphate buffer (2.5 mL) were added PhI(OAc)2 (986 mg) and AZADO (4.3
mg, 0.028 mmol) at 0 °C. The resultant mixture was gradually warmed to
room temperature, stirred for 19 h and then quenched with saturated
aqueous Na2S2O3. The resulting solution was extracted with EtOAc (3
times). The organic layer was washed with brine, dried over MgSO4 and
filtered. The solution was concentrated and the residue was purified with
flash column chromatography (EtOAc/hexane = 1/9) to afford carboxylic
acid 7a. Colorless oil, (77.3 mg, 0.386 mmol, 76%). [α]D17 = 21 (c =
1.48, CHCl3); IR (film) ν 2958, 2935, 1702, 1466,1372, 1281, 1151, 999
cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 0.85 (3H, d, J = 6.7 Hz), 0.89 (3H, d, J
= 6.7 Hz), 1.08 (3H, d, J = 6.7 Hz), 1.20-1.30 (1H, m), 1.43 (6H, s),
1.47-1.62 (1H, m), 2.90-3.02 (1H, m); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ18.0,
21.8, 21.9, 22.0, 23.3, 25.4, 39.9, 43.2, 56.1; 180.0, 212.1; HRMS (FAB)
calcd for C11H20NaO3 [M+Na]+223.1305, found 223.1307.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM buffered solution (phosphate) used in stage 1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Total Synthesis and Complete Structural Assignment of Yaku'amide A
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
